,title,link,text,language,family
0,Nafsan language - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nafsan_language,"The Nafsan language, also known as South Efate or Erakor, is a Southern Oceanic language spoken on the island of Efate in central Vanuatu. As of 2005, there are approximately 6,000 speakers who live in coastal villages from Pango to Eton.","Efate, South",Austronesian
