3,"Efate materials, primary historical sources, and recordings ...",https://researchdata.edu.au/efate-materials-primary-pangpang-erakor/,"South Efate documents, keyboarded versions of early texts written in South Efate. NT3-NadusIskei and NT3-TusiFe are the first books from Efate. NT3-catechism is the Efatese primer catechism and hymn book from 1911, text and images of the original. NT3-kenesis is Keyboarded from Genesis translated by Rev. J.Cosh (1874) NT3-scripturehistory, 1923,Scripture History: Efate New Hebrides 1923. NT3 ...","Efate, South",Austronesian
4,"Guide to materials in Nafsan, South Efate",https://www.nthieberger.net/sefate.html,"This page lists materials in and about Efate (Vanuatu), in particular, the south Efate language or Nafsan. It links to historical translations as well as more recent work I have undertaken with Nafsan speakers.","Efate, South",Austronesian
5,South Efate (Vanuatu),https://researchdata.edu.au/south-efate-vanuatu/12701,"Records in this collection were made during fieldwork, mainly in Erakor Village, Efate, Vanuatu since 1996. They consist of audio recordings of South Efate speakers, originally on audio cassettes (hence there are often A and B sides of a single item). There is a total of over 40 hours of language material, and the collection includes time-aligned transcripts in Elan for many recordings, and ...","Efate, South",Austronesian
6,"Efate, South language resources | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/languages/erk,"Efate, South language resources. Listing of people groups speaking Efate, South. Efate, South dialects and alternate names. Bible and ministry resource availability.","Efate, South",Austronesian
7,OLAC resources in and about the South Efate language,http://www.language-archives.org/language/erk,"ONLINETopics in the grammar and documentation of South Efate, an Oceanic language of Central Vanuatu. Nick Thieberger. 2005. Pacific And Regional Archive for Digital Sources in Endangered Cultures (PARADISEC). oai:paradisec.org.au:NT2-PHD ONLINEEfatese primer catechism and hymn book, 1911.","Efate, South",Austronesian
8,"ABVD: Efate, South (Eratap)",https://abvd.eva.mpg.de/austronesian/language.php?id=1110,"A Database of Basic Austronesian Vocabulary Seen an error? Please let us know: hand left right leg/foot to walk road/path to come to turn to swim dirty dust skin back belly bone intestines liver breast shoulder to know, be knowledgeable to think to fear blood head neck hair nose to breathe to sniff, smell mouth tooth tongue to laugh to cry to vomit to spit to eat to chew to cook to drink to ...","Efate, South",Austronesian
9,"A Dictionary of Nafsan, South Efate, Vanuatu: M̃p̃et Nafsan ... - JSTOR",https://www.jstor.org/stable/j.ctv1w36q4k,"In addition, the book gives an overview of the Nafsan sound system, provides a list of existing literature on the language dating back to early missionary translations, and includes maps of Efate locating nearly 200 place names. Readers will also find South Efate cultural knowledge embedded in the explanations of the Nafsan words and their usages.","Efate, South",Austronesian
